    "result_text": "Green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, all tests pass.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe GET response is an `OwnerDto` generated from `openapi.yml` and populated by `OwnerMapper`, which already derives `displayName` via a `@Mapping` expression. I added `initials` the same way:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field).\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one `@Mapping` line on `toOwnerDto`:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \\\".\\\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n   `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`.\n\n## Why this keeps structural impact low\n\n- I put the behaviour on `toOwnerDto`, whose cyclomatic complexity is 1 and whose surrounding class (a MapStruct interface of trivial abstract methods) has tiny `WMC_other` \u2014 instead of adding a method to the `Owner` entity, a large class whose `WMC_other` (the `getPet` loops, sorting, etc.) would have dominated the cost.\n- The change is a single added annotation line (CC 1 \u00d7 1 line), across just 2 files, and mirrors the existing `displayName` convention exactly, so no new pattern was introduced.",
